-----BEGIN PGP PUBLIC KEY BLOCK-----
REPLACE_ME_WITH_YOUR_PUB_KEY

One-time setup for the maintainer:

  1. Generate (or reuse) a GPG key tied to security@kiln3d.com:
       gpg --quick-generate-key 'Kiln Maintainer <security@kiln3d.com>' ed25519 sign 2y

  2. Export the public half as ASCII-armored:
       gpg --armor --export security@kiln3d.com > .well-known/maintainer.pub.asc

  3. Write the fingerprint to the companion file:
       gpg --fingerprint security@kiln3d.com \
         | awk '/ = /{gsub(" ",""); print $NF}' \
         | tr -d '=' \
         > .well-known/maintainer.pub.sha256

  4. Configure git to sign tags with this key:
       git config --local user.signingkey <KEY-ID>
       git config --local tag.gpgSign true

  5. Commit both files.  The public half is meant to be public;
     the PRIVATE half NEVER goes anywhere near the repo — it lives
     in the Keys folder (cold storage) and the local GPG keyring.

Until step 2 runs, this file is a placeholder and
scripts/verify_release.sh will exit with an explanatory FAIL rather
than a cryptic gpg error.
-----END PGP PUBLIC KEY BLOCK-----
